WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.768
-Welcome back, everybody!
We're hanging out

00:00:02.768 --> 00:00:05.171
with Will Ferrell and Paul Rudd,
right here on Thanksgiving!

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.572
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:09.308
On Thanksgiving, thank you
so much for being here.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:10.476
I want to talk about
"The Shrink Next Door."

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:12.211
By the way, it's fascinating.
I love it.

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:16.949
It's funny, it's dark,
it's real.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:18.551
It's based on a true --
well, it's not real --

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.686
you're acting in it.
-Right.

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:23.089
-But it's based on a real thing
and real guys.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.357
-Yeah.
-And a real situation.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.460
-Real starry of Marty Markowitz,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.664
who decided to try therapy
for the first time in his life,

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.967
had some issues,
and 27 years later,

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:38.604
woke up and realized
that the therapist,

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.573
played by Paul,
had forced him

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.110
to kind of divorce himself
from his entire family,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.847
his business, his every --
and it was just kind of

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.982
like he'd fallen into a cult.
-It's a crazy story.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:53.486
How did you hear about this?
-It was a podcast.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:57.756
There was a really popular
podcast of the same name,

00:00:57.756 --> 00:01:01.727
and I think, when it came out,
I was listening it to it,

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:05.098
Will was listening to it.
-Did you get to meet the guy?

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.866
-We did.
-Yeah.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.135
-We spent a whole day with him.
Hung out at his --

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.338
Had this Hamptons house,
throw all these parties at,

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.740
that the doctor
took over the house

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.109
as if it was his own,

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.244
and he lived there
as a groundskeeper.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.847
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:25.150
Each story gets more bizarre
as they go along.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.019
-Did you ask him, like --

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.088
I don't know
even what to ask him.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:32.958
Like, why would you --
-Yeah, we kind of --

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.660
We're like,
"How did this happen?"

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.895
And he's like, "Well..."

00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:39.966
It was like, "Yeah,
death by a thousand cuts."

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:43.135
Just over time,
he just didn't realize

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:45.004
till he woke up
kind of too late.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.507
-Wow. It's just unbelievable.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.375
But you both do
a fantastic job together.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.078
Is it hard to do dramatic scenes
with each other?

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.445
Because you've been
in "Anchorman."

00:01:53.445 --> 00:01:55.715
"Anchorman 2," right?

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.817
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:00.286
You guys work
very well together.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.922
-I think that --
I think we liked it.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.992
-Yeah.
-And we were kind of

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.293
goofing around
when we were setting up

00:02:08.293 --> 00:02:10.563
for shots and things like that.
-When you're off-screen.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:15.001
-Yeah, but I think we both liked
the idea of playing something

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.837
that people might not --
-We already had a shorthand

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.439
with each other
and, yeah, made it easy.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:23.409
-i appreciate you
being on the show tonight.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:26.512
Not only is it Thanksgiving,
but we had a talent night here,

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.580
and we had a young man
came out earlier

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:34.020
sing "Tiny Dancer" Elton John.
-We heard about that.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.989
-He was great,
and people really liked him,

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:38.958
but he got heckled
by two people in the audience.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.461
-Oh, did he?
-You filmed the people heckling?

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.429
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.165
-Well, there's thousands of
cameras the future,

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:50.169
so basically right now
we're living in an Oculus.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:54.574
I don't even know if you're here
or if you're augmented reality.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.542
-Right, right, right.
-You know, I don't know...

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.512
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.714
-So, that was --
-Those were real.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.917
-Unfortunately, but they
couldn't have been.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.920
I didn't know at the time.
-Please don't eat that berry.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.190
Paul, stop!
Paul, seriously, stop!

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.957
I have no idea
what those things are.

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:14.960
I don't know if they're real.
-They're Styrofoam.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.131
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.432
-But they're not bad.
-They're not bad.

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:24.436
-So, you let the show --

00:03:24.436 --> 00:03:28.007
you let the hecklers
go on and on and on?

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:30.142
You didn't kick them out?
-You know, it's funny,

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:31.543
I was in hair and makeup.
-Oh, you weren't here.

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:33.145
-No, I didn't see it.

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:36.182
I was backstage
doing hair and makeup.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:39.152
I do it for other --
for different people.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:41.954
And I do hair and makeup
for different people.

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:44.157
[ Laughter ]
And it was fun.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:47.560
And I just -- you know?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.763
So, yeah, I was
just kind of doing that.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:53.232
[ Laughter ]
And, uh...

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:57.737
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.006
There you go.
-Maybe it got better.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.974
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:05.577
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It's still not good.

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:07.146
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:08.547
Here's Will Ferrell
and Paul Rudd

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.483
in "The Shrink Next Door."
Take a look at this.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.051
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.118
-Do we want people
to come to our parties

00:04:13.118 --> 00:04:14.520
and enjoy themselves,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.822
or do you want them
to feel uncomfortable?

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:18.991
-No, I want them
to enjoy themselves.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:22.462
-Do you want to invite people
to take advantage of you?

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.630
-Hmm?
-Like Debbie did?

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:28.767
Like Phyllis did?
Kathy, to a certain extent?

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:32.605
-No, of course not.
-I didn't think so.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:37.543
You know
I'm doing this for you.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:41.113
To protect you.

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:44.784
We don't care, but
